<title>FRANCE: Algeria passes on 75,000 T wheat import tender.</title>
<headline>Algeria passes on 75,000 T wheat import tender.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria has passed up offers in a tender for the import of 75,000 tonnes of optional-origin milling wheat for April and May because prices offered were too high, European grain exporters said on Friday.</p>
<p>Exporters also said they expected Algeria to place another tender for the wheat soon, possibly next week.</p>
<p>&quot;Offers were submitted but they considered them too high. I assume they may re-tender soon,&quot; one exporter said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think Algeria did a &quot;pricing&quot; operation and will come back next week,&quot; another exporter said.</p>
</text>
